_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/pulls/51794","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/51794","diff_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/51794.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/51794.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"This commit changes where the REST API specs are read. The REST API \r\nspec is required to run the REST YAML tests and are currently copied\r\nto every project that has REST YAML tests. \r\n\r\nThe REST API specs are now copied to the build directory of the root\r\ngradle project under a \"rest-spec-api-current\" directory. Since\r\neach module or plugin (including all x-pack plugins) can contribute\r\nto the REST API spec, they too are copied to the common directory. \r\nThe result is a single directory created during the build which \r\nincludes the full REST API spec. A system property has been \r\nintroduced to allow the testing framework to know where this common\r\ndirectory lives on disk. \r\n\r\nAdditionally, the BWC based tests continue to copy the API \r\nand tests locally since they are special cases of the REST \r\nYAML testing. \r\n\r\n-------\r\n\r\nNote - this change related (but not dependent) to how the REST testing strategy https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/51816 will work. For example, that testing plans to use a \"rest-spec-api-prior\" directory for it's REST specs.  ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/51794/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/51794/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/comments/581852913","html_url":"https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/issues/51816#issuecomment-581852913","issue_url":"https://api.g